1. What is a Locator?
    A locator is a mechanism used by Selenium to identify a particular HTML element on a webpage.
    It contains:
      - Username text box.
      - Password text box.
      - Login button.
      - Forgot password link.

    Suppose you want Selenium to enter a username.
    How does Selenium know which text box to use?
    We provide a locator to identify that particular element.
  
    Example:
    driver.findElement(By.id("username")).sendKeys("SeleniumUser");


2. Types of Selenium Locators

Your HCL module covers these seven locator strategies:

                Locator	                        What it uses
                ID	                        Element's id attribute
                Name	                      Element's name attribute
                ClassName	                  Element's class attribute
                TagName	                    HTML tag name
                LinkText	                  Exact visible text of a link
                PartialLinkText	            Part of a link's visible text
                XPath	                      Path or expression to locate an element
                CSS Selector	              CSS-based element selection
